            <h3>The Studio</h3>
            <p>In-person lessons take place in a detached, finished private studio at my residential property in East Nashville. The exact address and arrival instructions are provided after enrollment and appointment confirmation.</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Dedicated entrance</li>
                <li>Private bathroom</li>
                <li>Professional recording and monitoring equipment</li>
                <li>Hands-on student workstation</li>
                <li>Space for a parent or guardian to observe</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="lesson-photo-placeholder">Studio photo placeholder</div>
            <p>Cats live on the property but are kept outside the studio during lessons. Please mention any significant animal allergies before scheduling.</p>

            <h3>For Parents</h3>
            <p>Parents and guardians are welcome to observe lessons. Students under 16 must have a parent or authorized adult remain on the property.</p>
            <ul>
                <li>A parent or guardian completes enrollment and manages payment for students under 18.</li>
                <li>Parents are included in scheduling and substantive communication.</li>
                <li>Emergency contact information is required.</li>
                <li>Private social-media communication is not used.</li>
                <li>Students are not transported by the instructor.</li>
                <li>Photography, recordings, testimonials, and public sharing require separate written permission.</li>
                <li>A current background check is available to parents upon request.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>The studio is maintained as a professional, substance-free learning environment with clear safety, hearing-protection, and conduct policies.</p>

            <h3>FAQ</h3>
            <div class="lesson-faq-item">
                <div class="lesson-heading">What ages do you teach?</div>
                <p>I primarily teach students age 14 and older. Younger students may be considered depending on their interests, maturity, and previous musical experience.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lesson-faq-item">
                <div class="lesson-heading">Does a student need previous experience?</div>
                <p>No. Complete beginners are welcome, as are experienced musicians who are new to recording or production.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lesson-faq-item">
                <div class="lesson-heading">Which software do you teach?</div>
                <p>I teach Ableton Live and Pro Tools directly. Most recording, production, and mixing principles also transfer to other DAWs.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lesson-faq-item">
                <div class="lesson-heading">Does a student need their own computer or equipment?</div>
                <p>Not to begin. Students can use the studio system during lessons. Regular access to a computer and DAW will become helpful as they progress.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lesson-faq-item">
                <div class="lesson-heading">Can students bring their own music?</div>
                <p>Yes. Students are encouraged to bring original songs, recordings, mixes, demos, and unfinished projects. I can also provide exercises and practice material.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lesson-faq-item">
                <div class="lesson-heading">What is the cancellation policy?</div>
                <p>At least 24 hours' notice is required to reschedule without charge. Complete payment, cancellation, and studio policies are provided before enrollment.</p>
            </div>

